    "result_text": "Both the targeted test and the full suite pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. `HouseholdNormalizer.java`** \u2014 reworked the household key\n- `householdId` is now the **first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`** (separator changed from `\\n` to `|`, digest truncated to 12 chars).\n- The comparison key now keys on `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`; last name is still trimmed/whitespace-collapsed/lower-cased, postcode compared as given (null \u2192 empty).\n\n**2. `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 routed everything through the computed id\n- `householdIdFor(...)` now passes `postcode` instead of `address`, so duplicate detection and the household-size input (`countHouseholdMembers` \u2192 `householdSize`) both key off the deterministic id automatically.\n- Added `rejectHouseholdDuplicate(householdId, sharesHousehold)`: a create whose computed `householdId` already exists is rejected **409** \u2014 **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set, which now *only bypasses the block* (the id is already shared deterministically, nothing is \"linked\").\n- `markPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold)`: a declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is **never flagged** as a possible duplicate.\n\n**3. `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `DuplicateOwnerException` subtype so the existing advice renders it as a uniform 409 with `errors: [lastName, postcode]`.\n\n**4. `openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, `possibleDuplicate`, and `identityKey` descriptions/examples to reflect the (lastName, postcode) 12-char keying and the bypass-vs-declared-member semantics.\n\n## Behaviour now matches the spec\n- Same `lastName` + `postcode` \u2192 same `householdId` (deterministic, no coordination).\n- A second owner in that household \u2192 **409**, unless `sharesHousehold=true`, in which case it's created as a declared member and **not** flagged as a possible duplicate.\n- Different `lastName` (same postcode) \u2192 different `householdId`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` and the full suite are green.",
